{"author":{"id":"7674679dac9170669f752d932f8b5955b1d55717359e13b1c1e687003c7bb99f"},"ops":[{"type":3,"timestamp":1790010215,"nonce":"wYDoya3E6YKB8853/pPCCOnhRKU=","message":"Two corrections from the design review (doc/design/configurable-schema.md), because this ticket as written would do the wrong thing:\n\n1. NO formatVersion bump. entity/dag/operation_pack.go:233 rejects any version mismatch outright — no range, no upgrade path — so bumping 4-\u003e5 makes every pack already written unreadable, which is the whole store. Teaching the reader otherwise means editing pristine entity/dag. It is also unnecessary: adding an op type is already compatible both ways, because an unrecognised type falls through to dag.UnknownOperation, which applies as a no-op, skips validation and re-marshals its original bytes verbatim. New binaries read old packs; old binaries preserve new ops instead of corrupting them.\n\n2. 'common.Status open/closed goes away' is staged, not done here. It reaches 23 Go files across 10 packages, a hand-written GraphQL enum, and 27 webui TypeScript files. This ticket lands the field model complete, with SetStatusOp reinterpreted as setting the status field (no data migration) and Snapshot.Status kept as a derived projection — closed when the category is completed or canceled. Callers move to categories afterwards, one surface at a time; the webui half rides with f32ea71, which rewrites those views anyway.\n\nAlso lands here: the rank value encoding (441dcbb, LexoRank string sorted by (rank, id)), so the format does not have to change later.","files":null}]}